<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
	The admin module suite, across both renderers: every admin menu item and the actions behind it, in PrimeFaces (pf/,
	tablet; pf/10-phone-smoke.xml on a phone) and SmartClient (sc/). Run it only against a disposable server: it backs up,
	changes, truncates and restores the data. AdminSuiteSailIT runs it; so can SailRunIT (-Dsail.run=sail/admin/admin.suite.xml).

	The bracket, across both renderers: 00-precondition.xml (PrimeFaces) checks that no earlier run left its restore
	marker; 00-backup.xml (a workflow) clears the completed jobs list and backs up in PrimeFaces, then clears it again and
	backs up in SmartClient; 00-marker.xml (SmartClient) leaves the marker that the restore must remove. Every member
	requires the set-ups, so when one fails nothing else runs. 99-restore.xml (a workflow) first restores the newest backup
	(SmartClient's), once; then both renderers check the marker has gone and each deletes its backup; it runs
	last, after failures too, but only when the precondition and the backup passed (otherwise the newest backup could be
	another one).

	Members are independent: each signs in, makes what it needs with its own run token, and cleans up. None requires another.
	The order still matters for one thing: the 05-reports-misc.xml members check the backup job's row in the completed jobs
	list, and the 11-user-list.xml and 98-destructive.xml members clear that list, so both 11 members run after both 05
	members, the destructive members run after every other one, and sc/99-truncate.xml (SmartClient's Truncate) runs last,
	just before the restore. pf/07-reports.xml is a workflow of SmartClient and PrimeFaces legs (report design is
	SmartClient only; the Reports list and scheduling are PrimeFaces only). The 06 and 08 members share fixed contact names
	(their spreadsheets cannot hold the run token), and the 11 members a generated user name family, so neither pair may run at
	the same time; a suite runs its members one at a time.

	-Dsail.suite.only=pf/ or sc/ chooses one renderer's members, and -Dsail.suite.only=03 both 03 members; the bracket
	always runs, in both renderers.
	Each member's strategy is its own (Assert); -Dsail.testStrategy=Verify applies to the ordinary members, while the set-ups
	and the restore stay locked to theirs.
-->
<suite xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.skyve.org/xml/sail ../../../../main/java/schemas/sail.xsd"
		xmlns="http://www.skyve.org/xml/sail"
		xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
	<description>Exercises the admin module as a user would meet it: every admin menu item and the actions behind it, in both the PrimeFaces tablet UX/UI (with one smoke script on a phone) and the SmartClient desktop UX/UI. The members cover signing in and out, contacts and communications, security administration, DevOps tools, reports, import and export, tags, operations, the user list, and the destructive maintenance actions.

		The suite protects the data it changes. Three set-ups run first: one checks that no earlier run left its restore marker, one backs up the data in each UI, and one leaves a marker that only a restore can remove. Each member signs in as admin (or as a user it makes), makes what it needs with names unique to the run, and cleans up after itself. Last, a restore puts the backup back, and both UIs check that the marker has gone and the backups are deleted.

		A pass means every menu item opens and behaves in both UIs, each create, change and delete shows up where the user would look for it, and the data is back as the suite found it. If a set-up fails, no member runs.</description>
	<viewRoles user="sail{run}">
		<!-- 03-security-admin.xml makes this user in a group with these roles, then signs in as them -->
		<role>admin.BasicUser</role>
		<role>admin.ContactViewer</role>
	</viewRoles>
	<setUp file="00-precondition.xml"/>
	<setUp file="00-backup.xml"/>
	<setUp file="00-marker.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/01-session.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/02-contacts-communications.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/03-security-admin.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/04-devops.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/05-reports-misc.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/06-import-export.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/07-reports.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/08-tags-communications.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/09-operations.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/10-phone-smoke.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/01-session.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/02-contacts-communications.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/03-security-admin.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/04-devops.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/05-reports-misc.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/06-import-export.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/07-reports.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/08-tags-communications.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/09-operations.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/11-user-list.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/11-user-list.xml"/>
	<member file="pf/98-destructive.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/98-destructive.xml"/>
	<member file="sc/99-truncate.xml"/>
	<restore file="99-restore.xml" requires="00-precondition.xml 00-backup.xml"/>
</suite>
